<div xmlns:perseus="http://www.perseus.org/meta/perseus.rdfs#" xmlns:dctype="http://purl.org/dc/dcmitype/" xmlns:tufts="http://www.tufts.edu/" xmlns:alph="http://alpheios.net/namespaces/tei" class="alpheios-lex-text_container en">
    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n26008" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">διασῴζω</span></b> , <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>A.</b><i>preserve through</i> a danger, of persons, 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">Ἀπόλλωνα δ. κατακρύψασα</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Hdt.
					2.156
				</span></i>
			; 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">δ. πόλιν</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					E.
					<u>Ph.</u>
					783
				</span></i>
			; 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">δ. τινὰ ἐκ κινδύνων</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Isoc.
					1.23
				</span></i>
			:—
				Med.
			, <i>save for oneself,</i>
			
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">τὰ πλείστου ἄξια</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					X.
					<u>Cyr.</u>
					4.2.28
				</span></i>
			:—
				Pass.
			, <i><span class="en">
				Pl.
				<u>Ti.</u>
				22d
			</span></i>; <i>come safe through,</i>
			
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">τοὺς διασωθέντας</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Id.
					<u>R.</u>
					540a
				</span></i>
			, cf. <i><span class="en">
				<u>1 Ep.Pet.</u>
				3.20
			</span></i>, etc.; <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">διασῴζεσθαι ἐς . .</span>
			or <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">πρός . .</span>
			<i>to come safe</i> to a place, <i><span class="en">
				Th.
				4.113
			</span></i>, <i><span class="en">
				X.
				<u>An.</u>
				5.4.5
			</span></i>, etc.; <i>recover</i> from illness, <i><span class="en">
				Id.
				<u>Mem.</u>
				2.10.2
			</span></i>. </div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense2"><b>II.</b> of things,
				<i>preserve, maintain,</i>
			
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἀνδρὶ τἀμὰ δ. λέχη . .</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					E.
					<u>Hel.</u>
					65
				</span></i>
			; <i>keep in memory,</i>
			<i><span class="en">
				X.
				<u>Mem.</u>
				3.5.22
			</span></i>; 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">δ. πίστιν τινί</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Id.
					<u>HG</u>
					7.2.17
				</span></i>
			; 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">δ. τὸν πρῶτον λόγον</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Pl.
					<u>R.</u>
					395b
				</span></i>
			, cf. <i><span class="en">
				Arist.
				<u>Ph.</u>
				189b1
			</span></i>; 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">τὰ παλαιά</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Isoc.
					10.63
				</span></i>
			:—
				Med.
			, <i>preserve for oneself, retain,</i>
			<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">εὐδαιμονίαν, εὐτυχίαν,</span>
			<i><span class="en">
				Th.
				3.39
			</span></i>, <i><span class="en">
				5.16
			</span></i>; 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">δόξαν</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Lys.
					2.69
				</span></i>
			; 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">τὴν τῶν Μήδων μαλακίαν</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					X.
					<u>Cyr.</u>
					8.8.15
				</span></i>
			.</div>
